<h2>Overhead and Profit (O&amp;P)</h2>
<p>When a repair requires several trades, such as roofing, drywall, painting, electrical and flooring, a general contractor is usually needed to schedule and supervise the work. General contractor overhead and profit is commonly added to the estimate in that situation. If your loss clearly involves multiple trades and the estimate has no O&amp;P, it is a reasonable question to raise. Whether it applies depends on the complexity of the job and the policy.</p>

